/*  liveProbe -- IA-4's CENSUS CARRIER, 2026-08-07. Deliberately does nothing.

    The grammar is parsed at STARTUP, before a line of this file runs, so the
    liveness question is already answered by the time the sentinel prints. All
    this file has to do is prove the process got that far: a run that dies
    during grammar parsing prints no sentinel, and its silence must NOT be read
    as "the bind was not consumed" -- that is the whole vacuity hazard of a
    census whose negative reading is an ABSENCE.

    So the driver requires the sentinel before it records any row. Absent
    sentinel is a VOID row, never a dead one.  */
Start();
print "LIVEPROBE SENTINEL":;
stop();
